- ## guillotine
+ ## guillotine

- - `guillotine.Executable#fork[result]()` (and so `Command#fork` and `Pipeline#fork`) now takes
+ - `guillotine.Executable#fork[result]()` (e quindi `Command#fork` e `Pipeline#fork`) ora prende

-   `(using working: WorkingDirectory, environment: ambience.Environment)`;
+   `(using working: WorkingDirectory, environment: ambience.Environment)`;

-   `Executable#exec[result]()`
-   takes `(using computable: (result is Computable)^, working: WorkingDirectory, environment:
-   Environment)`; the inline `Executable#apply()` takes `environment: Environment` after `working`.
-   A call site with no `Environment` in scope no longer compiles. Supply the `Environment` the
-   processes should inherit: the invocation's (`environments.daemonClientEnvironment`, or
-   `Environment.provided` from a `Cli`) in a tool, `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` for the
-   previous behaviour. (#2180)
- - Semantics: when the given `Environment`'s new `entries` member is not `Unset`, the process is
-   started with exactly those variables, rather than the JVM's, and a command whose name contains
-   no `/` is first looked up on that environment's `PATH`, its absolute path replacing the name as
-   `argv[0]`; a name not found there is left to the JDK. When `entries` is `Unset` (an
-   `Environment` written as a lambda, say) the JVM's environment is inherited as before.
-   `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` defines `entries`, so a process started under it gets the
-   JVM's environment, as before. (#2180)
+   `Executable#exec[result]()` prende `(using computable: (result is Computable)^, working:
+   WorkingDirectory, environment: Environment)`; l'`Executable#apply()` inline prende
+   `environment: Environment` dopo `working`. Un punto di chiamata senza un `Environment`
+   nell'ambito non compila più. Si fornisce l'`Environment` che i processi devono ereditare:
+   quello dell'invocazione (`environments.daemonClientEnvironment`, o `Environment.provided` da
+   un `Cli`) in uno strumento, `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` per il comportamento
+   precedente. (#2180)
+ - Semantica: quando il nuovo membro `entries` dell'`Environment` fornito non è `Unset`, il
+   processo viene avviato esattamente con quelle variabili, anziché con quelle della JVM, e un
+   comando il cui nome non contiene `/` viene prima cercato nel `PATH` di quell'ambiente, e il
+   suo percorso assoluto sostituisce il nome come `argv[0]`; un nome non trovato lì è lasciato al
+   JDK. Quando `entries` è `Unset` (per esempio un `Environment` scritto come lambda) l'ambiente
+   della JVM è ereditato come prima. `environments.javaBaseEnvironment` definisce `entries`,
+   quindi un processo avviato sotto di esso riceve l'ambiente della JVM, come prima. (#2180)

- ## honeycomb
+ ## honeycomb

- - `honeycomb.Node`, `honeycomb.Element`, `honeycomb.Comment`, `honeycomb.Doctype` and
-   `honeycomb.Fragment` moved into the `Html` companion, with their companion objects: they are
-   now `honeycomb.Html.Node`, `honeycomb.Html.Element`, `honeycomb.Html.Comment`,
-   `honeycomb.Html.Doctype` and `honeycomb.Html.Fragment` (so `Element.foreign` is
-   `Html.Element.foreign`). Each is removed from the `soundness` umbrella export, so the bare
-   names `Node`, `Element`, `Comment`, `Doctype` and `Fragment` no longer resolve through
-   `import soundness.*` or `import honeycomb.*`; write `Html.Element`, `Html.Fragment` and so on,
-   in types, constructor calls and patterns (`case Html.Element(label, attributes, children, _)`).
-   Behaviour unchanged. (#2167)
- - `honeycomb.TextNode` renamed to `honeycomb.Html.Text`, and `TextNode.foreign` to
-   `Html.Text.foreign`; `TextNode` removed, including from the `soundness` umbrella export.
-   Behaviour unchanged. Inside a scope that imports `Html.*`, the bare name `Text` now means this
-   node type rather than `anticipation.Text`; such imports should be replaced by qualified
-   references. (#2167)
- - `honeycomb.Honeycomb` (also exported as `soundness.Honeycomb`) removed. Its members,
-   `extractor`, `interpolator` and `attributes`, were unused duplicates of the macro
-   implementations in `honeycomb.internal`, which the `h""` interpolator and tag application
-   call; no replacement is needed. (#2173)
+ - `honeycomb.Node`, `honeycomb.Element`, `honeycomb.Comment`, `honeycomb.Doctype` e
+   `honeycomb.Fragment` spostati nell'oggetto compagno di `Html`, con i loro oggetti compagni: ora
+   sono `honeycomb.Html.Node`, `honeycomb.Html.Element`, `honeycomb.Html.Comment`,
+   `honeycomb.Html.Doctype` e `honeycomb.Html.Fragment` (quindi `Element.foreign` è
+   `Html.Element.foreign`). Ciascuno è rimosso dall'esportazione dell'ombrello `soundness`,
+   quindi i nomi nudi `Node`, `Element`, `Comment`, `Doctype` e `Fragment` non si risolvono più
+   tramite `import soundness.*` o `import honeycomb.*`; si scrive `Html.Element`,
+   `Html.Fragment` e così via, nei tipi, nelle chiamate ai costruttori e nei pattern
+   (`case Html.Element(label, attributes, children, _)`). Comportamento invariato. (#2167)
+ - `honeycomb.TextNode` rinominato in `honeycomb.Html.Text`, e `TextNode.foreign` in
+   `Html.Text.foreign`; `TextNode` rimosso, anche dall'esportazione dell'ombrello `soundness`.
+   Comportamento invariato. In un ambito che importa `Html.*`, il nome nudo `Text` indica ora
+   questo tipo di nodo anziché `anticipation.Text`; tali import vanno sostituiti da riferimenti
+   qualificati. (#2167)
+ - Rimosso `honeycomb.Honeycomb` (esportato anche come `soundness.Honeycomb`). I suoi membri,
+   `extractor`, `interpolator` e `attributes`, erano duplicati inutilizzati delle
+   implementazioni delle macro in `honeycomb.internal`, che l'interpolatore `h""` e
+   l'applicazione dei tag chiamano; non serve alcuna sostituzione. (#2173)

- ## hyperbole
+ ## hyperbole

- - `hyperbole.StackResolver` now takes `(using classloader: Classloader, working:
-   ambience.WorkingDirectory)`; the given `hyperbole.stackResolutions.tastyStackResolution` (also
-   `soundness.stackResolutions.tastyStackResolution`) has type `(Classloader, WorkingDirectory) =>
-   StackTrace.Resolver`, was `Classloader => StackTrace.Resolver`; and the extension
-   `StackTrace#resolved` takes `(using Classloader, WorkingDirectory)`. A source path that TASTy
-   records relative to `-sourceroot` is now resolved against the given `WorkingDirectory`, where it
-   was resolved against `workingDirectories.javaBaseWorkingDirectory` (`user.dir`). Supply the
-   directory the code was compiled under. (#2180)
+ - `hyperbole.StackResolver` ora prende `(using classloader: Classloader, working:
+   ambience.WorkingDirectory)`; il given `hyperbole.stackResolutions.tastyStackResolution` (anche
+   `soundness.stackResolutions.tastyStackResolution`) ha tipo `(Classloader, WorkingDirectory) =>
+   StackTrace.Resolver`, era `Classloader => StackTrace.Resolver`; e l'estensione
+   `StackTrace#resolved` prende `(using Classloader, WorkingDirectory)`. Un percorso di sorgente
+   che TASTy registra relativo a `-sourceroot` è ora risolto rispetto alla `WorkingDirectory`
+   fornita, dove era risolto rispetto a `workingDirectories.javaBaseWorkingDirectory`
+   (`user.dir`). Si fornisce la directory in cui il codice è stato compilato. (#2180)

